Blender look — theme-blender

This extension is the MODEL EDITOR's, and it lives in the vgai-engine
repository (`packages/model-editor/workbench/extensions/theme-blender/`). It is
copied into a Code-OSS checkout at build time by
`scripts/workbench/overlay.mjs`, so in a built workbench it sits under
`extensions/theme-blender/` beside Code-OSS's own MIT extensions. This
extension's own manifest, theme JSON and layout defaults are MIT.

ITS PRODUCT ICON FONT IS NOT. `producticons/blender-icons.otf` is a build of
Blender's own icon artwork.

  Blender
  Copyright (C) Blender Authors
  Licensed under the GNU General Public License, version 2 or later.
  <https://www.blender.org/about/license/>

WHAT THE FONT CONTAINS. `producticons/blender-product-icon-theme.json` maps 37
product-icon ids onto 35 glyphs, and those glyphs are compiled from
`@vgai/blender`'s `contributions/blender.icons.json` in this repository (the
theme file records the source file's sha256). That icon set is part ours and
part Blender's: 197 of its 346 glyphs are MACHINE-TRACED, byte for byte, from
Blender's own vector sources — `release/datafiles/icons_svg/*.svg`, 188 distinct
files — by an affine transform onto a 16-unit grid that re-proportions,
re-strokes and re-centres nothing. A traced glyph IS Blender's drawing, and
baking it into an OpenType font does not change that: the outlines in this OTF
are Blender's outlines, and they are a derivative work of GPL-2.0-or-later
artwork. Per-glyph provenance — `ICON_*` name, source SVG path and sha256 — is
`packages/blender/contributions/blender.icons.traced.json`.

THE LICENCE THAT APPLIES. Exercising Blender's "or later", the traced artwork in
`producticons/blender-icons.otf` is conveyed under the GNU General Public
License, version 3 or later. Neither the MIT grant on the Code-OSS tree this
extension is built into, nor this repository's own AGPL grant, extends to it,
and nothing in this extension may be read as relicensing Blender's artwork: the
copyright in it is Blender's authors' and is not Volter AI, Inc.'s to
relicense. No commercial licence Volter AI, Inc. offers reaches it (see
COMMERCIAL.md).

  SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT AND GPL-3.0-or-later

A product that cannot carry the GPL replaces `blender-icons.otf` with its own
drawings and re-points `blender-product-icon-theme.json` at them; the theme
colours and the layout defaults in `package.json` are unaffected.

THE UI FONT. The Blender look also loads `Inter.woff2`, which this product
carries beside its contribution (`packages/model-editor/workbench/src/media/`)
and the overlay copies into the workbench under
`src/vs/workbench/contrib/vgaiProduct/browser/media/`. It is the Inter typeface,
copyright (c) 2016 The Inter Project Authors, under the SIL Open Font License
1.1. Its notice and full licence text are in `ThirdPartyNotices.txt` at the
Code-OSS fork's root, and its component entry is in that tree's
`cgmanifest.json` — the two files that describe what a BUILT workbench contains.
